WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:08.600
Single sign-on, or SSO, allows users to authenticate through a central identity provider and access multiple applications that trust that provider.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:14.900
The application or service relying on that identity information is often called a service provider or relying party.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:21.280
Federation is the trust relationship that lets one system rely on identity information from another.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:25.900
This can improve consistency, but it also concentrates risk in identity configuration.

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:31.880
SAML, OAuth, and OpenID Connect are often discussed together, but they serve different roles at a high level.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:35.860
SAML is commonly used for enterprise federation and signed assertions.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:43.280
OAuth is primarily about delegated access, where a client receives permission to access resources on behalf of a user or service.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:50.140
OpenID Connect adds an identity layer on top of OAuth-style flows for sign-in and identity claims.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:54.120
Scopes and claims describe requested access and identity information.

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:56.980
A scope might represent delegated permission.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:01.920
A claim might state an identifier, group, assurance level, or other attribute.

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:06.940
Protocol data must be validated carefully by the application or platform that consumes it.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:15.240
Teams should understand protocol roles and trust boundaries, while relying on mature libraries and identity platforms rather than hand-rolling protocol behavior.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:22.340
Federation applies to enterprise identity, customer identity, service-to-service authentication, and workload identity.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:36.160
It can make authentication more consistent and easier to govern, but misconfigured trust, overly broad application assignment, weak claim handling, stale certificates, or excessive delegated access can affect many systems at once.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:40.860
Federation needs governance, review, monitoring, and lifecycle management.
